  "narrative": {
    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** Lulus is purposefully reorienting toward higher-margin demand, compressing order volumes and lifting return rates but with higher average order values. An aggressive markdown‑driven reset of casual apparel and footwear clears unwanted inventory, while wholesale gains traction as a growth channel. Gross margins are recovering despite top‑line softness. Short interest has nearly vanished and an activist believes the turnaround is substantially undervalued.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Management, led by CEO Crystal Landsem, is executing a deliberate turnaround: resetting assortments, tightening order economics, and expanding wholesale. The company reaffirmed its full‑year outlook, signaling confidence. Notably, activist Friedland Enterprises pivoted from demanding board changes to praising operational progress, strengthening management’s credibility. Ongoing debt reduction and expense discipline further demonstrate a steady, execution‑focused hand.",
